@page "/docs/accessibility/names-and-announcements"

@* Names: fields' labels, the components that throw without a name (artifacts/izzyblazor-a11y-inventory
   section 1.3), icons and images. Announcements: LiveRegion, Announcer, alerts, toasts, tables, combobox,
   carousel, chat, busy states (section 1.4). *@

<ArticlePage Section="accessibility" Slug="names-and-announcements">
    <Lead>
        Every control has a name that screen readers read, and IzzyBlazor requires one wherever WCAG or ARIA does. When
        something changes without a full reload, such as a filtered count, a saved form or a new toast, the change is
        announced.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <Heading Level="2">Labels on fields</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Every field renders a <Code>label</Code> linked to its control, and links its hint and errors with
            <Code>aria-describedby</Code>. The label comes from <Code>Label</Code>. Without it, the label comes from the
            model property's <Code>[Display]</Code> or <Code>[DisplayName]</Code> name, or else from the property's name
            split into words (<Code>FirstName</Code> becomes "First name"). To hide the label but keep it for screen readers, set
            <Code>HideLabel</Code>.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Components that require a name</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            These components throw an exception on their first render when their name is missing, so you notice at once.
            Most of them show only an icon or a picture, with no text for a screen reader to read:
        </TextBlock>
        <Table Items="Required" Caption="Components that require a name" Size="ControlSize.Sm" Class="site-params site-params-wrap" Bordered="false">
            <Columns>
                <TemplateColumn Title="Component"><Anchor Href="@($"docs/components/{context!.Id}")">@context.Name</Anchor></TemplateColumn>
                <TemplateColumn Title="Requires">@context.Requires</TemplateColumn>
            </Columns>
        </Table>
        <TextBlock>
            Where ARIA makes a name optional, so does IzzyBlazor. Landmarks get a default name from
            <Anchor Href="docs/common/text">IzzyText</Anchor>, such as "Breadcrumb" and "Pagination". When a page has two of the
            same kind, set <Code>Label</Code> on each.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Icons and pictures</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem>An <Anchor Href="docs/components/icon">Icon</Anchor> is hidden from screen readers unless you give it a <Code>Label</Code>, so it never repeats the text beside it.</ListItem>
            <ListItem>An <Anchor Href="docs/components/avatar">Avatar</Anchor> is read as its <Code>Name</Code>.</ListItem>
            <ListItem>Alerts and toasts show their status with an icon as well as a color. A <Code>Badge</Code>'s <Code>Status</Code> is color only, so its text must say what it means.</ListItem>
            <ListItem>A chart is named by its <Code>Title</Code>, and its Show data table lists every value.</ListItem>
        </List>

        <Heading Level="2">What components announce</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem>Danger and warning alerts are announced as soon as they appear. Other alerts are announced politely. A <Code>Banner</Code> isn't announced, because it's there when the page loads. To announce one that appears later, set <Code>Announce</Code>.</ListItem>
            <ListItem>Toasts are announced politely. Their timers pause while the user hovers over or focuses them. Error toasts stay until the user dismisses them.</ListItem>
            <ListItem>A table's "1–10 of 50" and its filter status are announced when they change. So is every move made with the keyboard or a menu: a DataGrid's rows and columns, a ListView's or DropZoneGroup's items, a PickList's items and a TileLayout's tiles. A CopyButton announces "Copied".</ListItem>
            <ListItem>A combobox announces "No matches", and a carousel announces its new slide. A chat announces "Replying" and then "Reply complete". It reads a message from someone else with the author's name.</ListItem>
            <ListItem>A loading button sets <Code>aria-busy</Code>, and screen readers read its <Code>LoadingLabel</Code>. A <Code>Spinner</Code> is read as its <Code>Label</Code>, and a <Code>Progress</Code> announces its value.</ListItem>
            <ListItem>A PasswordField announces a Caps Lock warning. It also announces when all its requirements are met.</ListItem>
        </List>

        <Heading Level="2">Announcing your own changes</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            To announce a change the components don't know about, such as a list's new count after a filter, set a
            <Anchor Href="docs/components/live-region">LiveRegion</Anchor>'s <Code>Text</Code>. Screen readers read it each
            time it changes. Render the LiveRegion with the page, even while it's empty, because a region that appears with
            its text already in it isn't read.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            To announce the result of an action, such as "Revoked the invite", call <Code>Announcer.Announce</Code>. On
            <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">static pages</Anchor>, <Code>AnnouncerRegion</Code> sends the message in
            the response to the form post, and a <Code>ToastRegion</Code> includes an AnnouncerRegion. A redirect drops the
            message, so after a redirect, show a toast instead.
        </TextBlock>
    </ChildContent>
</ArticlePage>

@code {
    private sealed record Named(string Name, string Id, string Requires);

    private static readonly Named[] Required =
    [
        new("IconButton", "icon-button", "Label"),
        new("FloatingButton", "floating-button", "Label"),
        new("SpeedDial", "speed-dial", "Label, and a Label on each SpeedDialAction"),
        new("SplitButton", "split-button", "Label"),
        new("ToggleButton", "toggle-button", "Label when IconOnly"),
        new("Image", "image", "Alt, or Alt=\"\" for a decorative picture"),
        new("QrCode", "qr-code", "Label, or Decorative when the text beside it describes it"),
        new("Chart and every other chart", "chart", "Title, or TitledBy to name it with your own heading"),
        new("Sparkline", "sparkline", "Label"),
        new("Gauge, LinearGauge", "gauge", "Label, and a Label on each GaugePointer"),
        new("Stat with a Sparkline", "stat", "Label or SparklineLabel"),
        new("Carousel", "carousel", "Label"),
        new("Chat", "chat", "Label"),
        new("Collapsible", "collapsible", "Label, or your own Trigger"),
        new("FilterSelect, FilterCheckbox, FilterDate", "filter-form", "Label"),
        new("Menu", "menu", "Label for its button, or your own Trigger"),
        new("Popover", "popover", "Label for its button, or your own Trigger"),
        new("ContextMenu", "context-menu", "Label"),
        new("MenuSub", "menu", "Label"),
        new("Tab", "tabs", "Label"),
        new("TabLink", "tab-nav", "Label"),
        new("Card with Href", "card", "Title, which becomes the link text"),
        new("ColumnBand", "table", "Title"),
        new("Tile in an Editable TileLayout", "tile-layout", "Title or Label, which names its Move handle"),
    ];
}
